  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting eutectic high-entropy alloy has a hierarchical microstructure of dual-phase lamellar colonies.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Internal lamellar boundaries foster dislocation pile-ups that cause local stress concentrations and microcracking.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated alloy has low room-temperature tensile ductility and undergoes brittle failure because of dislocation pile-ups at internal lamellar boundaries.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging can induce coherent precipitation in a high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A single optimized aging treatment will form uniformly distributed coherent nanoprecipitates specifically along the target alloy's internal lamellar interfaces.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment is conceptually similar to treatments producing δ lamellae and γ″ particles.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The aging treatment can be applied after solidification without altering the primary eutectic morphology.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boundary nanoprecipitates will act as dislocation absorbers.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boundary nanoprecipitates will redistribute stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent precipitate interfaces will allow dislocations to bypass or shear through boundary regions rather than accumulate there.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced dislocation accumulation will lower local stress concentrations and suppress microcrack initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coherent precipitates will increase strength through precipitation hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will increase tensile elongation into the 10–15% range relative to the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will retain or increase yield strength and ultimate tensile strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strength may increase by approximately 1 GPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted benefits apply under room-temperature tensile loading at conventional strain rates.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::rubric_card::000::2d68b747c3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The benefits depend on maintaining an appropriate precipitate size and distribution that remain coherent with the matrix.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oversized or incoherent precipitates may compromise the strength–ductility benefits.",
      "field": "boundary",
